hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16051","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said, Said al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Salil, from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi, Ismail said once, from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi, from a man of his people, he said, I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of the roads of Madinah, and upon him was a cotton waist-wrapper with loose fringe, and I said, upon you peace, O Messenger of Allah, and he said: Upon you peace is the greeting of the dead, upon you peace is the greeting of the dead, upon you peace is the greeting of the dead, peace be upon you, peace be upon you, twice or thrice, thus he said. I asked about the waist-wrapper, and I said, where do I wear it, so he bared his back with the bone of his leg, and said: Here wear it, and if you refuse, then here, lower than that, and if you refuse, then here, above the ankles, and if you refuse, then Allah, mighty and majestic, does not love every arrogant boaster. He said, and I asked him about kindness, and he said: Do not belittle any kindness, even that you give the rope tie, even that you give the sandal thong, even that you pour from your bucket into the vessel of one seeking water, even that you remove a thing from the road of the people that harms them, even that you meet your brother with your face cheerful to him, even that you meet your brother and greet him, even that you comfort the lonely in the land. And if a man reviles you with what he knows in you, and you know the like in him, do not revile him, so its reward is for you, and its sin upon him. And what pleases your ear to hear, act upon it, and what displeases your ear to hear, avoid it."
